<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42367" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sălŏmon</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sŏlŏmon</span></b> ),
			ōnis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σαλωμών, Σαλομών, Σολομών</span> [],
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Solomon</i>,
				<i>son of David</i>, <i><span class="en">Prud.
				Hamart. 581</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juvenc. 2,
			717</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Alcim. 6, 387</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Lact. 4, 16</span></i>. —Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sălŏmōnĭus</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sŏlŏm-</span></b> ), a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Solomon</i>, <i>Solomon</i>'<i>s</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">templum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 4, 13 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also called saxa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Apoth. 512</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Să-lŏmōnĭăcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj. (<b>poet.</b>), <i>of Solomon</i>, <i>Solomon</i>'<i>s</i>: templum, Sid.
			poët. Ep. 4, 18; Ven. Carm. 1, 11, 1.</div>
